Enforcement Decree of the Special Act on Support for Pyeongtaek-si, etc. Following the Relocation of United States Forces Korea Bases

Article 1 (Purpose)
The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters delegated by the Special Act on Support for Pyeongtaek-si, etc. Following the Relocation of United States Forces Korea Bases and matters necessary for its enforcement. <Amended on September 17, 2009>

Article 2 (Scope of Local Governments)
"Local government prescribed by Presidential Decree" in subparagraph 5 of Article 2 of the Special Act on Support for Pyeongtaek-si, etc. Following the Relocation of United States Forces Korea Bases (hereinafter referred to as the "Act") means Gimcheon-si. <Amended on September 17, 2009>

Article 3 (Scope of Surrounding Areas)
"Areas prescribed by Presidential Decree" in subparagraph 8 of Article 2 of the Act means the following areas:
1. Areas within three kilometers of the boundaries of the granted areas under subparagraph 3 of Article 2 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "granted areas") that are publicly notified by the Mayor of Pyeongtaek-si and the Mayor of Gimcheon-si (hereinafter referred to as the "Mayor of Pyeongtaek-si, etc.") in consultation with the Minister of National Defense;
2. Eups or myeons, part of which falls within a granted area, that are publicly notified by the Mayor of Pyeongtaek-si in consultation with the Minister of National Defense.

Article 4 (Scope of Internationalization Planning Districts)
"Areas developed with an area prescribed by Presidential Decree" in subparagraph 9 of Article 2 of the Act means areas developed by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport with an area of at least 2,500,000 square meters pursuant to Article 21 of the Act. <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013>

Article 5 (Disposal of Returned Property Released from Grant, etc.)
(1) Where the Minister of National Defense intends to receive a transfer of management from the original management authority in order to dispose of State property under Article 8 (1) 2 of the Act pursuant to the State Property Act, the Minister shall consult with the original management authority. <Amended on July 27, 2009>
(2) Where an agreement is not reached through consultation under paragraph (1), the general management authority under the State Property Act shall make the decision. <Amended on July 27, 2009>
(3) A building layout plan under Article 8 (2) of the Act may be substituted by a building layout plan prepared and maintained by United States Forces Korea.

Article 5-2 (Organization and Operation of the United States Forces Korea Base Relocation Project Group)
(1) The head and deputy head of the United States Forces Korea Base Relocation Project Group under Article 8-2 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Project Group") shall be appointed by the Minister of National Defense from among public officials in general service belonging to the Senior Civil Service of the Ministry of National Defense, general- or flag-rank officers, or fixed-term public officials. <Amended on November 20, 2013; September 5, 2017>
(2) The head shall oversee the affairs of the Project Group and direct and supervise its personnel under orders of the Minister of National Defense.
(3) The deputy head shall assist the head and act on behalf of the head where the head is unable to perform the duties of the office due to unavoidable circumstances.
(4) Where necessary for the operation of the Project Group, the Minister of National Defense may request relevant administrative agencies and relevant institutions, organizations, etc. to dispatch their public officials, executive officers, or employees.
(5) Matters necessary for the operation of the Project Group, other than those prescribed in this Decree, shall be determined by the Minister of National Defense.

Article 5-3 (Advisory Members)
(1) Where necessary to hear expert opinions or conduct investigations or research in connection with the performance of the Project Group's duties, the head may have relevant experts, such as relevant public officials, executive officers or employees of relevant institutions or organizations, and university professors, serve as advisory members.
(2) Advisory members shall be commissioned by the Minister of National Defense upon the recommendation of the head.

Article 5-4 (Remuneration and Allowances)
(1) Remuneration for public officials, executive officers, or employees dispatched to the Project Group shall be paid by their original institutions.
(2) Public officials, executive officers, or employees dispatched to the Project Group may be paid allowances, travel expenses, and other necessary expenses within budgetary limits.
(3) Where advisory members under Article 5-3 provide advice on the United States Forces Korea base relocation project, they may be paid allowances and travel expenses within budgetary limits.

Article 5-5 (Functions of the Project Group)
"Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree for the promotion of United States Forces Korea facilities projects, etc." in Article 8-2 (3) 4 of the Act means the following matters:
1. Requests for and execution of project budgets related to United States Forces Korea facilities projects, etc.;
2. Consultation with United States Forces Korea in connection with United States Forces Korea facilities projects, etc.;
3. Cooperation in affairs with relevant central administrative agencies and local governments in connection with United States Forces Korea facilities projects, etc.;
4. Other matters that the Minister of National Defense deems necessary for the promotion of United States Forces Korea facilities projects, etc.

Article 6 (Expenditures from the Special Account for the Relocation of United States Forces Korea Bases)
"Funds necessary for other projects prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 9 (4) 10 of the Act means funds falling under any of the following subparagraphs:
1. Expenses for the return, management, and disposal of returned property released from grant (limited to State property), including surveying and appraisal expenses;
2. Funds necessary for projects recommended by the Mayor of Pyeongtaek-si, etc. that the Minister of National Defense deems consistent with the purposes of expenditures from the Special Account for the Relocation of United States Forces Korea Bases.

Article 7 (Formulation of Regional Development Plans)
(1) Where the Minister of the Interior and Safety intends to formulate a regional development plan pursuant to Article 14 (1) of the Act, the Minister shall prepare a draft regional development plan and send it to the Governor of Gyeonggi-do and the Mayor of Pyeongtaek-si. <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013; November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>
(2) The Governor of Gyeonggi-do and the Mayor of Pyeongtaek-si who receive a draft regional development plan under paragraph (1) shall, except in special circumstances, send a written opinion to the Minister of the Interior and Safety within 30 days from the date of receipt. <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013; November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>
(3) Upon receiving written opinions under paragraph (2), the Minister of the Interior and Safety shall review and reflect those opinions and finalize the regional development plan following consultation with the heads of relevant central administrative agencies. <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013; November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>
(4) The head of a relevant central administrative agency requested to engage in consultation under paragraph (3) shall, except in special circumstances, send a written opinion to the Minister of the Interior and Safety within 30 days from the date of the request, and the Minister of the Interior and Safety who receives the written opinion shall reflect it in the regional development plan unless there is a special reason not to do so. <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013; November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>
(5) "Important matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the latter part of Article 14 (3) of the Act means the following matters:
1. A change in land area exceeding 30 percent of the land area required for implementing the finalized regional development plan;
2. A change in the budget exceeding 30 percent of the budget required for implementing the finalized regional development plan;
3. A change in a project plan that entails a change in the objectives of the finalized regional development plan.

Article 8 (Formulation of Annual Development Plans)
(1) Where the Mayor of Pyeongtaek-si intends to formulate an annual development plan each year pursuant to the former part of Article 15 (1) of the Act, the Mayor shall prepare a draft development plan and send it to the Governor of Gyeonggi-do by November 30 of the second year preceding the year of implementation. <Amended on April 27, 2006>
(2) The Governor of Gyeonggi-do who receives a draft development plan under paragraph (1) shall, except in special circumstances, send a written opinion to the Mayor of Pyeongtaek-si within 30 days from the date of receipt.
(3) The Mayor of Pyeongtaek-si shall prepare an annual development plan reflecting the opinion received under paragraph (2) and submit it to the Minister of the Interior and Safety by January 31 of the year preceding the year of implementation. <Amended on April 27, 2006; February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013; November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>
(4) A development plan under paragraph (3) shall include the following matters, and relevant documents shall be attached when the plan is submitted to the Minister of the Interior and Safety: <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013; November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>
1. Order of priority of projects under the development plan;
2. Basic objectives and outline of the projects;
3. Financing plan for each project;
4. Implementation performance of the previous year's projects and an analysis of their results;
5. Details of project costs;
6. Project implementation periods;
7. Effects of the projects.
(5) The Minister of the Interior and Safety who receives a development plan under paragraph (3) shall approve it by March 31 of the year preceding the year of implementation, following consultation with the heads of relevant central administrative agencies. <Amended on April 27, 2006; February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013; November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>
(6) Article 7 (4) shall apply mutatis mutandis to consultation under paragraph (5). In such cases, "regional development plan" shall be construed as "development plan."
(7) Where an approved development plan is to be amended pursuant to the latter part of Article 15 (1) of the Act, the procedures under paragraphs (1) through (6) shall be followed, but the processing period for each stage shall not exceed 30 days.
(8) "Important matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the latter part of Article 15 (1) of the Act means the following matters:
1. A change in land area exceeding 30 percent of the land area required for implementing the approved development plan;
2. A change in the budget exceeding 30 percent of the budget required for implementing the approved development plan;
3. A change in a project plan that entails a change in the objectives of the approved development plan.

Article 9 (Approval for Implementation of Pyeongtaek-si Development Projects)
(1) A person who intends to obtain approval for implementing a Pyeongtaek-si development project (hereinafter referred to as a "project" in this Article) pursuant to Article 17 (1) and (3) of the Act shall submit to the Mayor of Pyeongtaek-si a project plan and an investment plan that include the following matters. In such cases, documents prescribed by relevant statutes and regulations, such as an environmental impact assessment report, shall be attached:
1. Name and purpose of the project;
2. Details and scale of the project;
3. Estimated project costs and methods of financing;
4. Project implementation period;
5. Project site (including a location map);
6. Plan for securing the necessary land;
7. Relevant drawings.
(2) "Important matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 17 (2) of the Act means the following matters:
1. Name and purpose of the project;
2. Estimated project costs and methods of financing;
3. Project implementation period;
4. Project site.
(3) A person who intends to obtain approval for a change to a project pursuant to Article 17 (2) and (3) of the Act shall submit to the Mayor of Pyeongtaek-si the project plan and investment plan as amended with respect to the matters specified in the subparagraphs of paragraph (1).
(4) "Standards prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 17 (4) of the Act means detailed standards established and publicly notified by the Mayor of Pyeongtaek-si with respect to the following matters:
1. Measures to prevent environmental pollution;
2. Adequacy of the capacity to implement the project;
3. Securing financial resources for investment;
4. Other matters, such as the degree of contribution to local industries.
(5) Where the Mayor of Pyeongtaek-si receives an application for approval of a project or approval of a change under paragraph (1) or (3), the Mayor shall process the application within 30 days from the date of receipt.
(6) Where the Mayor of Pyeongtaek-si grants approval for implementation pursuant to Article 17 (4) of the Act, the Mayor shall publicly notify the following matters pursuant to paragraph (5) of that Article:
1. Name of the project;
2. Name and address of the project implementer and the name of its representative;
3. Purpose and outline of the project;
4. Project implementation period;
5. Project site.
(7) Where a person prescribed in subparagraphs 1 through 3 of Article 16 of the Act intends to consult with the Mayor of Pyeongtaek-si on a project plan pursuant to Article 17 (7) of the Act, the person shall submit to the Mayor of Pyeongtaek-si a draft project plan including the matters specified in the subparagraphs of paragraph (1) and documents prescribed by relevant statutes and regulations, such as an environmental impact assessment report.
(8) Where a person prescribed in subparagraphs 1 through 3 of Article 16 of the Act prepares a project plan in consultation with the Mayor of Pyeongtaek-si pursuant to paragraph (7), the person shall publicly notify the matters specified in the subparagraphs of paragraph (6).

Article 10 (Budget Requests)
(1) Pursuant to Article 19 of the Act, the heads of relevant central administrative agencies shall request from the Minister of Planning and Budget the budgets for projects under their jurisdiction included in development plans under Article 8 of this Decree: Provided, That the Minister of the Interior and Safety shall request the budgets to be subsidized by the State for projects implemented by Gyeonggi-do and Pyeongtaek-si that do not fall under the jurisdiction of the heads of relevant central administrative agencies. <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013; November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017; December 30, 2025>
(2) The head of a relevant central administrative agency or the Minister of the Interior and Safety shall endeavor to ensure that the costs of projects under their jurisdiction included in development plans under Article 8 are reflected in the budget in priority to other projects. <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013; November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

Article 11 (Designation, etc. of Internationalization Planning Districts)
(1) The heads of relevant central administrative agencies, the Governor of Gyeonggi-do, and the Mayor of Pyeongtaek-si who receive a request for consultation on the designation of an internationalization planning district (including changes thereto; hereinafter the same shall apply) pursuant to Article 21 (2) of the Act shall send a written opinion to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport within 30 days from the date of receipt of the request, except in special circumstances. When the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport consults with the heads of relevant central administrative agencies, the Governor of Gyeonggi-do, and the Mayor of Pyeongtaek-si, the Minister shall attach the following documents. In such cases, the heads of relevant central administrative agencies, the Governor of Gyeonggi-do, and the Mayor of Pyeongtaek-si shall verify the cadastral maps and forest land maps of the internationalization planning district through the joint use of administrative information under Article 36 (1) of the Electronic Government Act. <Amended on February 29, 2008; November 2, 2010; March 23, 2013>
1. A location map (at a scale of 1:25,000);
2. A topographic map showing the boundaries of the internationalization planning district and the reasons for determining those boundaries (at a scale of 1:5,000);
3. Deleted <November 2, 2010>;
4. Data on the current status of farmland and forest land to be incorporated;
5. Photographs showing the current status of the internationalization planning district.
(2) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport and the Mayor of Pyeongtaek-si intend to hear the opinions of residents and relevant experts on the designation of an internationalization planning district pursuant to Article 21 (3) of the Act, they shall publicly announce the name, location, area, etc. of the internationalization planning district they intend to designate and make the relevant documents available for public inspection for at least 14 days from the date of the public announcement. <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013>
(3) Residents and relevant experts who have opinions on a proposed designation of an internationalization planning district publicly announced pursuant to paragraph (2) shall submit their opinions to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport or the Mayor of Pyeongtaek-si within 30 days from the date of the public announcement, and the Mayor of Pyeongtaek-si shall immediately forward the opinions received to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport. <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013>
(4) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport designates an internationalization planning district pursuant to Article 21 (4) of the Act, the Minister shall publicly notify the following matters in the Official Gazette. In cases of a change, the reasons for the change shall also be publicly notified. <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013>
1. The name of the internationalization planning district;
2. The location of the internationalization planning district;
3. The date of designation of the internationalization planning district;
4. The area designated as an internationalization planning district;
5. The purpose of designating the internationalization planning district.
(5) The term "changes to minor matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso of Article 21 (2) of the Act means an increase or decrease in the area of an internationalization planning district within 10 percent of the area of that district. <Newly inserted on October 26, 2007>
(6) Where the area of an internationalization planning district is increased pursuant to paragraph (5) and military base and military installation protection zones under the Military Bases and Installations Protection Act, agricultural promotion areas under the Farmland Act, or other areas, districts, etc. under other statutes are included, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall consult in advance with the heads of relevant central administrative agencies. <Newly inserted on October 26, 2007; amended on February 29, 2008; September 22, 2008; March 23, 2013>

Article 12 (Approval, etc. of Internationalization Planning District Development Projects)
(1) Where an implementer of an internationalization planning district development project (hereinafter referred to as a "development project") intends to obtain approval of an internationalization planning district development plan (including approval of changes thereto; hereinafter the same shall apply) pursuant to Article 23 (1) of the Act, the implementer shall prepare an application for approval of the internationalization planning district development plan containing the following matters and submit it to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport. <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013>
1. The type and name of the development project (including a location map);
2. The location and area where the development project is to be implemented;
3. The implementation period of the development project;
4. Plans for securing and using the required land;
5. Where any designation, approval, etc. is deemed granted pursuant to the subparagraphs of Article 24 of the Act, the details thereof;
6. The name and address of the development project implementer and the name of its representative;
7. Other matters determined by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport as necessary for implementation of the development project.
(2) A development project implementer shall apply to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport for approval of an internationalization planning district development plan within two years from the date on which the designation of the internationalization planning district is publicly notified pursuant to Article 11 (4). The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall determine whether to grant approval within three months from the date of receipt of the application for approval and notify the development project implementer in writing. <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013>
(3) The term "important matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the latter part of Article 23 (1) of the Act means the following matters:
1. A change of more than 30 percent in the area of land required for implementation of the approved internationalization planning district development plan;
2. A change of more than 30 percent in the budget required for implementation of the approved internationalization planning district development plan;
3. A change to a project plan that entails a change to the objectives of the approved internationalization planning district development plan.
(4) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport approves an internationalization planning district development plan, the Minister shall publicly notify the following matters pursuant to Article 23 (4) of the Act: <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013>
1. The name of the development project;
2. The name and address of the development project implementer and the name of its representative;
3. The purpose and outline of the development project;
4. The implementation period of the development project;
5. The site of the development project;
6. Details of the location, lot number, land category, area, ownership, and rights other than ownership of the land, etc. to be expropriated or used, and the names and addresses of the owners and holders of rights thereto.

Article 12-2 (Supply of Land within Internationalization Planning Districts)
(1) Article 13-2 of the Enforcement Decree of the Housing Site Development Promotion Act shall apply mutatis mutandis to the procedures and methods for supplying developed land under Article 24-3 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "developed land").
(2) The development cost under Article 24-3 (2) of the Act shall be the sum of the following costs:
1. Land costs;
2. Land charges;
3. Land development expenses;
4. Infrastructure installation costs;
5. Direct labor costs;
6. Relocation measures costs;
7. Selling expenses;
8. General administrative expenses;
9. Capital costs;
10. Other costs incurred in connection with the development project.
(3) Where a development project implementer supplies developed land at or below its development cost pursuant to Article 24-3 (2) of the Act, the supply price shall be the price determined in consultation with the Governor of Gyeonggi-do.

Article 13 (Types of Business for Which New Factories May Be Established)
The term "types of business prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso of Article 25 (1) of the Act means those specified in Annex 1.

Article 14 Deleted <October 26, 2007>

Article 15 (Special Support for Educational Finances)
The scope of special support through local education finance grants pursuant to Article 28 of the Act shall be support projects necessary for improving educational conditions, operating curricula, providing education and training, and making appointments at schools of each level at or below the high school level located in Pyeongtaek-si in connection with the development of Pyeongtaek-si.

Article 16 (Subsidy Rates for National Subsidies)
(1) The subsidy rate for projects eligible for subsidies pursuant to Article 29 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "support subsidy rate" in this Article) shall be the standard subsidy rate under Article 9 (1) 2 of the Subsidy Management Act (hereinafter referred to as the "standard subsidy rate" in this Article) plus 20 percentage points. <Amended on April 28, 2016>
(2) Where adding 20 percentage points to the standard subsidy rate pursuant to paragraph (1) yields a rate exceeding 80 percent, the support subsidy rate shall be 80 percent. However, where the standard subsidy rate is at least 80 percent, the support subsidy rate shall be that standard subsidy rate.

Article 17 (Priority Installation of Public Facilities)
The term "other facilities prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of Article 30 of the Act means the following facilities: <Amended on April 27, 2006>
1. Railroads, power transmission lines, plazas, green spaces, public open spaces (公共空地), common utility conduits (公同溝), detention basins (遊水池), fire prevention facilities, windbreak facilities, flood prevention facilities, erosion control facilities, tidal protection facilities, sewerage systems, ditches, and embankments;
2. Parking lots and sports grounds installed by administrative authorities.

Article 18 (Installation of Facilities for the Convenience of Local Residents)
(1) The Mayor of Pyeongtaek-si, etc. shall formulate a plan for the installation and use of facilities for the convenience of local residents in consultation with the Minister of National Defense pursuant to Article 32 (1) of the Act.
(2) A plan formulated pursuant to paragraph (1) shall include the following matters:
1. The purpose of installing facilities for the convenience of local residents;
2. The outline and types of facilities for the convenience of local residents to be installed;
3. The project implementation plan and necessity for each facility;
4. Financing plans and investment plans.
(3) The Minister of National Defense who receives a request for consultation pursuant to paragraph (1) shall send a written opinion to the Mayor of Pyeongtaek-si, etc. within 30 days from the date of receipt of the request, except in special circumstances, and the Mayor of Pyeongtaek-si, etc. who receives the written opinion shall incorporate it unless there is a special reason not to do so.
(4) Where the Mayor of Pyeongtaek-si, etc. formulates a plan pursuant to paragraph (1), the Mayor of Pyeongtaek-si, etc. shall notify the Minister of National Defense of its contents without delay and apply for disbursement of support funds by April 30 of the year preceding the year in which the relevant facility project is to be implemented.
(5) The Minister of National Defense shall notify the Mayor of Pyeongtaek-si, etc. of the decision on the support funds for which the Mayor of Pyeongtaek-si, etc. has applied pursuant to paragraph (4) within 60 days from the date of receipt of the application for disbursement of support funds.

Article 19 (Relocation Measures and Livelihood Measures)
(1) The Minister of National Defense shall establish and implement relocation measures under the Act on Acquisition of and Compensation for Land, etc. for Public Works Projects for relocatees under Article 33 (1) of the Act.
(2) The term "tenants, etc. prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 33 (1) of the Act means the following persons: <Amended on January 25, 2012>
1. Residents who are actual cultivators and who have continuously owned or leased at least 3,600 square meters of farmland from October 30, 2003 until the date on which a sales contract is concluded or an adjudication on expropriation is rendered for land or residential buildings incorporated into granted areas for the implementation of a United States Forces Korea facilities project (hereinafter referred to as the "date of conclusion of a contract, etc."), at least two-thirds of whose farmland is incorporated into granted areas (hereinafter referred to as "residents of neighboring areas"): Provided, That residents of neighboring areas shall be limited to owners of residential buildings who reside in an Eup, Myeon, or Dong adjoining the boundary of a granted area or in an area within Pyeongtaek-si that is not a granted area;
2. Owners of residential buildings who have continuously resided in granted areas from October 30, 2003 until the date of conclusion of a contract, etc.: Provided, That persons eligible for relocation measures under Article 40 of the Enforcement Decree of the Act on Acquisition of and Compensation for Land, etc. for Public Works Projects shall be excluded;
3. The following persons who have continuously engaged in business or farming in granted areas from October 30, 2003 until the date of conclusion of a contract, etc.:
(a) Persons eligible for business compensation or livestock farming compensation due to the implementation of a United States Forces Korea facilities project;
(b) Persons who cultivate or grow crops or perennial plants on at least 1,000 square meters of farmland or engage in agriculture for at least 90 days a year;
(c) Persons who install facilities, such as plastic greenhouses, covering at least 330 square meters on farmland and cultivate or grow crops therein;
4. Tenants who, as of the public announcement of approval of the project plan under Article 4 of the Act on National Defense and Military Installations Projects, have continuously resided for at least one year in buildings owned by other persons within granted areas.
(3) The Minister of National Defense may establish and implement the following relocation measures and livelihood measures for relocatees and tenants, etc. under paragraphs (1) and (2) (hereinafter referred to as "relocatees, etc."):
1. Supply of housing sites to residents of neighboring areas, etc.;
2. Supply of commercial sites or sites for the construction of neighborhood living facilities (hereinafter referred to as "commercial sites, etc.");
3. Supply of rental housing.
(4) The selection of persons eligible for relocation measures and livelihood measures under paragraph (3) and the terms of supply shall be governed by the criteria prescribed in Annex 2.
(5) Where the Minister of National Defense intends to implement relocation measures and livelihood measures under paragraphs (1) and (3), the Minister may request the implementer of a Pyeongtaek-si development project under Article 16 of the Act, the implementer of an internationalization planning district development project under Article 22 of the Act, and the implementer of a housing site development project under Article 7 of the Housing Site Development Promotion Act to supply housing sites, commercial sites, etc. and rental housing (hereinafter referred to as "housing sites, etc."). In such cases, where housing sites are supplied to relocatees under paragraph (1), the supply price may be set at or below the development cost.
(6) Where the Minister of National Defense has established relocation measures and livelihood measures under paragraph (3), the Minister shall notify eligible persons or their universal successors that they should apply for the supply of housing sites, etc.: Provided, That where the address or place of residence of an eligible person or their universal successor is unknown, public notice shall be given at least twice in each of two or more daily newspapers, at intervals of at least one week.
(7) Where an eligible person or their universal successor fails to apply for supply within three months from the date of receipt of the notice under paragraph (6) or the date of the last public notice, that person shall be deemed to have waived the application for supply.
(8) Article 40 (1), (2), and (6) of the Enforcement Decree of the Act on Acquisition of and Compensation for Land, etc. for Public Works Projects shall apply mutatis mutandis to the supply of housing sites to residents of neighboring areas, etc. under paragraph (3) 1 of this Article. <Amended on April 17, 2018>
(9) Where necessary to supply housing sites under paragraphs (1) and (3) 1, the Minister of National Defense may propose to the Mayor of Pyeongtaek-si, etc. the formulation of urban or Gun management plans, etc. <Amended on April 10, 2012>

Article 20 (Entrustment of Land Purchase Affairs, etc.)
Where the Minister of National Defense entrusts affairs concerning compensation for losses, such as the purchase of land, etc. and the implementation of relocation measures for relocatees, etc., under Article 33 (4) of the Act, Article 43 (2) through (5) of the Enforcement Decree of the Act on Acquisition of and Compensation for Land, etc. for Public Works Projects shall apply mutatis mutandis to the scope of the entrusted affairs, etc. <Amended on December 3, 2008>

Article 21 (Livelihood Support for Relocatees, etc.)
The Mayor of Pyeongtaek-si, etc. may take the following measures to support the livelihoods of relocatees, etc. under Article 33 (5) of the Act:
1. Vocational training and job placement services for the persons concerned and their children, where the persons concerned wish to change occupations;
2. Assistance in finding substitute land and training in farming, where the persons concerned wish to continue farming.

Article 22 (Special Relocation and Resettlement Grants, etc.)
(1) The Minister of National Defense may pay special relocation and resettlement grants and special livelihood stabilization grants to provide support necessary for relocation and resettlement or livelihood stabilization under Article 33 (6) of the Act.
(2) The selection of persons eligible for the special relocation and resettlement grants and special livelihood stabilization grants under paragraph (1) and the amounts of the grants shall be governed by the criteria prescribed in Annex 3.

Article 23 (Amounts, Management, and Operation of Grants, etc.)
(1) The total amount of grants provided to Pyeongtaek-si and Gimcheon-si under Article 33 (7) of the Act shall not exceed 30 billion won, and the grants shall be used for the following purposes:
1. Relocation support projects, such as loans for lump-sum rental deposits, payment of moving expenses, and subsidies for housing purchase costs for low-income persons, for relocatees, etc.;
2. Living expense support projects, such as support for meal expenses, heating expenses, and communications expenses for low-income persons, older persons, etc.;
3. Projects to support income generation for relocatees, etc., such as subsidies for the costs of developing advanced farming complexes, installing communal warehouse facilities, and purchasing shared agricultural machinery;
4. Welfare support projects, such as the construction of village halls, installation of sports facilities, and creation of parks within resettlement complexes;
5. Other support projects for relocatees, etc. that the Mayor of Pyeongtaek-si, etc. deems necessary in the course of implementing a United States Forces Korea facilities project, including the resolution of civil complaints.
(2) Matters concerning the management and operation of the grants under paragraph (1) shall be prescribed by ordinances of Pyeongtaek-si and Gimcheon-si.
(3) The Mayor of Pyeongtaek-si, etc. shall formulate a plan for the use of the grants under paragraph (1), and shall submit the plan for the following year to the Minister of National Defense by April 30 of each year.
(4) The plan for the use of grants under paragraph (3) shall include the purpose and outline of each project, the required budget, the implementation period of each project, beneficiaries, and other matters necessary for the projects.
(5) The Minister of National Defense shall review the plan submitted by the Mayor of Pyeongtaek-si, etc. under paragraph (3) and notify the Mayor of Pyeongtaek-si, etc. of the decisions on the amounts of grants, etc. within 60 days from the date of receipt of the plan. In such cases, the Minister of National Defense may provide different amounts of support in consideration of the proportion of relocatees, etc.

Article 23-2 (Transfer of Village Facilities for Common Use Free of Charge)
(1) The term "facilities for common use prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as village halls and communal warehouses" in Article 33-2 (1) of the Act means the following facilities:
1. Village halls;
2. Communal warehouses;
3. Facilities for older persons and children (老幼者施設);
4. Village communal workshops;
5. Physical fitness centers;
6. Memorial halls.
(2) The term "residents' communities, such as village associations, prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 33-2 (1) of the Act means residents' communities, such as village associations, that are unincorporated associations whose members comprise all or some of the residents of administrative districts, such as Dongs and Ris.
(3) The supplementary registration under Article 33-2 (3) of the Act shall contain the following statement: "This facility is real property acquired under the Special Act on Support for Pyeongtaek-si, etc. Following the Relocation of United States Forces Korea Bases, and, without the consent of the head of Pyeongtaek-si, etc. referred to in subparagraph 5 of Article 2 of that Act, no transfer of the facility, creation of limited real rights, or any other act restricting ownership, such as attachment, provisional attachment, or provisional disposition, is permitted."

Article 24 (Support through Local Allocation Tax)
Where the Mayor of Pyeongtaek-si, etc. makes a request under Article 34 of the Act on the grounds of special fiscal needs arising from special needs related to local issues, the Minister of the Interior and Safety may, following an annual review, grant special allocation tax under Article 9 of the Local Allocation Tax Act within the limits of the resources available for its operation. <Amended on February 29, 2008; March 23, 2013; November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

Article 25 (Preferential Employment of Relocatees and Residents of Surrounding Areas)
(1) When implementing a project, the project implementer under Article 35 (1) of the Act shall take measures necessary to give priority to hiring relocatees and residents of surrounding areas, such as preparing hiring plans by sector and requesting the Mayor of Pyeongtaek-si, etc. to recommend persons for employment.
(2) Upon receiving a request for employment recommendations under paragraph (1), the Mayor of Pyeongtaek-si, etc. shall take necessary measures, such as recommending relocatees and residents of surrounding areas for employment.
(3) Where Pyeongtaek-si, etc. restrict eligibility to participate in bidding under Article 35 (2) of the Act to persons whose principal place of business is within Pyeongtaek-si, etc. or persons participating in bidding jointly with such persons, necessary matters concerning such restriction may be prescribed by ordinance of the relevant local government. <Newly inserted on January 8, 2008>

Article 26 (Identification Certificates for Entry by Relevant Public Officials)
The identification certificate under Article 37 (2) of the Act shall be as prescribed in attached Form 1.

Article 26-2 Deleted. <March 7, 2023>

Article 27 (Criteria for Imposing Administrative Fines)
The criteria for imposing administrative fines under Article 39 (1) of the Act shall be as prescribed in Annex 4.

